96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (This report documents the Adaptive Study Planner Agent, a command line application that models a student's topic level mastery and produces a daily study plan using search over candidate study actions. The project was built for the Fundamentals of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning course and is meant to demonstrate, in a working system rather than slides, how an intelligent agent can combine a probabilistic model, a supervised learning component and an informed search algorithm to make a practical recommendation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (The system does not use any external AI service. All reasoning, from the Bayesian mastery update to the plan search, runs locally using standard Python and scikit-learn.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 65 0 R
/T (2. Problem Statement)
/E (2. Problem Statement)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Students preparing for several subjects at once usually decide what to study by feel rather than by any structured estimate of what they actually know. This means weak topics that need the most attention often get the least, especially once an exam date is close and time pressure sets in. The project addresses this by keeping an explicit, updatable estimate of mastery per topic, and using that estimate, along with difficulty, importance, exam urgency and time since last review, to decide what to study each day.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
