245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The project is implemented in plain Python 3 with scikit-learn and numpy as the only third party dependencies. Data classes \(models.py\) represent StudentProfile, Subject and Topic, each with a to_dict/from_dict pair for JSON serialization. The mastery module works directly on Topic objects and has no knowledge of the CLI. The ML predictor and the planner similarly take plain data \(dicts or Topic/Subject objects\) and have no direct dependency on the storage or CLI layers, which is what made the automated tests possible without touching the filesystem beyond a disposable CSV.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (main.py contains only input handling, validation loops \(read_float, read_int, read_date\), and calls into the agent. All business logic - Bayesian updates, ML prediction, search - lives in src/.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
