254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (- Getting the beam search to behave correctly when a state has no remaining candidate actions \(for example, a profile with only one topic that has already hit its repeat limit\) required explicitly carrying that state forward instead of silently dropping it, which an early version of the planner did, leading to an empty search frontier and a crash. This was caught by the test suite \(test_generate_plan_creates_actions\) and fixed by tracking whether a state produced any expansion.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (- Balancing the utility function weights so that no single factor \(in particular exam urgency\) dominates the others took a few iterations of running the demo dataset and checking that both the weakest topic)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (and the most urgent exam got reasonable priority.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (- Deciding how much the forgetting mechanism should move mastery required care, since too aggressive a pull back makes long unstudied topics look artificially weak, and too weak a pull back makes the model ignore staleness entirely.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
