/Title (Generate a ranked, time bounded study plan for the current day. Replan after new assessment results and show what changed compared to the previous plan. Respect the student's daily time budget and avoid scheduling the same topic too many times in one plan.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 678 0 R
>>
endobj
702 0 obj
<<
/Title (The application follows a simple layered structure. The CLI layer \(main.py\) handles input/output only. It calls into an agent layer that owns the planning workflow, which in turn uses three focused modules for the Bayesian mastery model, the ML predictor and the search based planner. Persistence and analytics sit alongside as independent modules.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 680 0 R
/Next 703 0 R
>>
endobj
703 0 obj
<<
/Title (Data flows in one direction for reads: the CLI asks the agent for a plan, the agent asks the planner, the planner asks the ML predictor for a success probability per topic and reads mastery directly off the topic object. Writes \(recording an assessment\) go agent to mastery module, and the updated state is saved by storage.py after each CLI action.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 680 0 R
/Prev 702 0 R
>>
endobj
