710 0 obj
<<
/Title (The planner is a beam search over sequences of 20 minute study actions. The state is the remaining time budget, how many times each topic has already been used in this plan, and the actions chosen so far. At each step, every candidate \(subject, topic\) pair still under its repeat limit is scored with the utility function below, a new action is created, and the resulting state is added to the pool of candidates for the next step. The pool is sorted by total accumulated utility and trimmed to the beam width \(default 4\) before the next step. This bounds the search to beam_width x candidates work per step instead of growing combinatorially with the number of slots.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 705 0 R
/Next 711 0 R
>>
endobj
711 0 obj
<<
/Title (The search stops once the remaining time in every surviving partial plan is below one slot, or after a maximum number of actions. The highest total utility plan in the final pool is returned along with a trace of the best utility seen at each step, which is shown to the user as the 'search trace' line.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 705 0 R
/Prev 710 0 R
>>
endobj
