717 0 obj
<<
/Title (Bias and variance considerations: with only seven features and a linear model, the predictor sits on the higher-bias, lower-variance side, which is a reasonable choice for a small dataset since a higher variance model \(for example an unpruned decision tree\) would likely fit noise in only 300 training rows. The roughly 75 percent test accuracy is treated in the application as a moderately confident signal to blend into the planner's utility function, not as a precise probability.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 709 0 R
/Prev 724 0 R
>>
endobj
