724 0 obj
<<
/Title (Recent average score and current mastery have the largest positive weight, which matches the intuitive expectation that a student who has been doing well recently and already knows the topic reasonably well is more likely to have a successful next session. Days since last study has a negative weight, consistent with rustier topics being harder to succeed at immediately. The negative weight on exam_urgency reflects a pattern in the synthetic generation formula and should be read as a property of the training data, not a real claim that urgency itself makes a session harder; this is flagged here as a limitation of training on a synthetic formula rather than real behavioural data.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 709 0 R
/Prev 716 0 R
/Next 717 0 R
>>
